MID_LGV_1LED_c02_Moo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_Moo_m01_001: We have to head for Coris Mine. Fast!
MID_LGA_1LED_c02_Moo_m01: <BLN>Coris. Coris!
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B01_m01_001: I worked in Coris Mine, until I escaped. The\nconditions there were like nothing I've ever seen.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B01_m01_002: Everyone there—from hired workers to criminals and\npolitical prisoners—was forced to do hard labor.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B01_m01_003: Hmm... I knew nothing of a mine in the area.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B01_m01_004: That's no surprise. It's only been in operation since\nthe Cydonia Massacre a few years back.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B01_m01_005: And the mine's a closely kept secret. I hear they\neven kill people who can't work anymore.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B01_m01_006: What?! My mom's at a place like that?! Then we've\ngot to get there as fast as we can!
MID_LGA_1LED_c02_B01_m01: <BLN>It was awful.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B02_m01_001: Our last viceroy died in the siege, and his\nreplacement is horribly cruel.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B02_m01_002: Her name's Balboa. I hear she used to be an\nAragonian general.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B02_m01_003: Seems to like the view from her high horse.\nEvery day, you see her underlings treated like dirt.
MID_LGA_1LED_c02_B02_m01: <BLN>This town has really changed.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B03_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B03_B04_m01_001: You know what's strange? I can't remember the last\ntime I saw Viceroy Balboa around.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B03_B04_m01_002: Me neither, now that you mention it. I wonder if\nshe's holed up in Coris Mine again.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B03_B04_m01_003: I heard they brought in a bunch of furniture for her,\nso for all we know, it's cool and luxurious in there.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B03_B04_m01_004: In any case, I'm not complaining. The town's much\nmore peaceful and pleasant when she's not in it.
MID_LGA_1LED_c02_B03_m01: <BLN>It's strange.
MID_LGA_1LED_c02_B04_m01: <BLN>Now that you mention it...
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B05_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B05_m01_001: The way I heard it, there's buckets and buckets of\ngold to be gotten down in Coris Mine.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B05_m01_002: All you'd have to do is sneak in and nab a few\nnuggets, and you'd make out like a bandit.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B05_m01_003: Problem is, security's tight. Anyone tries to leave,\nthey get killed on sight.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B05_m01_004: Though I think there is someone in town who\nmanaged to escape.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B05_m01_005: If you wanted to find out more, you could do worse\nthan speaking to him.
MID_LGA_1LED_c02_B05_m01: <BLN>It's only a rumor...
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B06_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B06_m01_001: Here and there you still see marks and blemishes\nfrom the massacre four years ago.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B06_m01_002: Even the viceroy's office, which burned down in\nthe battle, still hasn't been restored.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B06_m01_003: They say Viceroy Guillermo's corruption was what\ncaused it, but...I don't know.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B06_m01_004: I just find it hard to believe he was corrupt. He was\na good viceroy, and widely adored.
MID_LGA_1LED_c02_B06_m01: <BLN>He was a good viceroy.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B07_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B07_m01_001: Everyone says that Viceroy Guillermo's daughter was\nextremely talented.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B07_m01_002: Her musical skill was recognized by Kalla's temple,\nand she was given the title Rose of Caelus.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B07_m01_003: But she went missing after the viceroy's office\nburned down, poor thing.
MID_LGA_1LED_c02_B07_m01: <BLN>Poor thing.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B08_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B08_m01_001: After the invasion, this region was incorporated into\nArago's territory.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B08_m01_002: And after all the Aragonians moved in, the makeup\nof the population changed quite a bit.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B08_m01_003: Whole swaths of the original residents were driven\nout by the newcomers.
MID_LGA_1LED_c02_B08_m01: <BLN>It's certainly changed.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B09_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B09_m01_001: This city still hasn't recovered from the invasion.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B09_m01_002: I participated in the siege—even started competing\nwith the other soldiers to grab loot.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B09_m01_003: And when General Balboa was appointed viceroy,\nI was ordered to stay garrisoned here.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B09_m01_004: I don't know... Sometimes it feels wrong living in the\ncity that I helped throw into chaos.
MID_LGA_1LED_c02_B09_m01: <BLN>It doesn't feel right.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B10_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B10_m01_001: I wonder why Viceroy Balboa's made so little effort\nto rehabilitate the city.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B10_m01_002: It's pretty ruthless to leave your own territory in such\na sorry state.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B10_m01_003: And meanwhile, she and her family are living lives of\nluxury thanks to spoils from the mines.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B10_m01_004: That strikes me as a pretty good recipe for popular\ndiscontent. Let's hope it doesn't spill over...
MID_LGA_1LED_c02_B10_m01: <BLN>That's ruthless.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B11_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B11_m01_001: The laborers here mine for gold, day in, day out,\nnot even allowed to go outside.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B11_m01_002: If you're not sleeping or eating, you're here. I don't\neven know when it's day and when it's night.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B11_m01_003: And if you leave, you're killed on the spot. There's\nonly one word for this place—hell.
MID_LGA_1LED_c02_B11_m01: <BLN>I'm in hell.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B12_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B12_m01_001: Why did I believe any of that bastard Bjor's\npromises? Why did I let him send me here?
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B12_m01_002: He promised me the moon and stars, and what I got\nwas this awful life.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B12_m01_003: If I ever make it out, I'll rip his head off and find\na nice, deep ditch to kick it into.
MID_LGA_1LED_c02_B12_m01: <BLN>This isn't what he promised.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B13_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B13_m01_001: I beg you... Please let me out. You must free me from\nthis place!
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B13_m01_002: I can't do it anymore. My body's worn out. One more\nminute of this and truly, I'll break...
MID_LGA_1LED_c02_B13_m01: <BLN>I can't keep doing it...
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B14_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B14_m01_001: There was a woman we had here—strong, confident\ntype. But it's been a second since I saw her.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B14_m01_002: She caused some kind of commotion in the mines\nthe other day.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B14_m01_003: I just hope she's OK. I'd be gutted if she was killed\nfor disobeying the guards...
MID_LGA_1LED_c02_B14_m01: <BLN>I hope she's OK.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B15_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B15_m01_001: There was a cave-in over in the western section last\nmonth, and dozens of people were buried alive.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B15_m01_002: But I can't die here. I have to make it to the end of\nmy contract and get all I'm owed.
MID_LGV_1LED_c02_B15_m01_003: And make it back home, of course. With enough\nmoney in my pocket to live a life of leisure!
MID_LGA_1LED_c02_B15_m01: <BLN>I can't die here.